WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.886
Day-to-Day Communication.

2
00:00:02.166 --> 00:00:06.155
Day 59 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Workplace phase.

3
00:00:07.905 --> 00:00:08.929
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:15.759
People judge you on the small things you do every day: the stand-up, the Slack reply, the PR description.

5
00:00:16.039 --> 00:00:20.220
These habits build your reputation faster than one big presentation.

6
00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:22.423
Part 1.

7
00:00:22.703 --> 00:00:23.791
Daily stand-up.

8
00:00:25.041 --> 00:00:25.852
Format.

9
00:00:26.132 --> 00:00:28.009
Here is a template you can copy.

10
00:00:28.289 --> 00:00:32.983
Yesterday: finished the coupon API, PR 212 in review.

11
00:00:33.263 --> 00:00:35.567
Today: integrate with cart, write tests.

12
00:00:35.847 --> 00:00:40.476
Blockers: need staging DB access, @Ops, can you help after stand-up?

13
00:00:43.326 --> 00:00:44.179
Rules:

14
00:00:44.459 --> 00:00:45.974
30 to 60 seconds.

15
00:00:46.254 --> 00:00:47.833
Outcomes, not activities.

16
00:00:48.113 --> 00:00:49.585
Take blockers offline.

17
00:00:50.935 --> 00:00:52.236
Weak versus strong.

18
00:00:52.516 --> 00:00:53.860
Here is a quick table:

19
00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:55.271
Weak, and Strong.

20
00:00:55.551 --> 00:00:58.665
Yesterday I was working on the bug, still working on it.:

21
00:00:58.945 --> 00:01:01.847
The login bug is narrowed to the token refresh.

22
00:01:02.127 --> 00:01:03.535
Fix by noon today.

23
00:01:03.815 --> 00:01:04.903
No blockers.

24
00:01:05.183 --> 00:01:06.164
(when you're stuck):

25
00:01:06.444 --> 00:01:08.343
I'm stuck on the PDF library.

26
00:01:08.623 --> 00:01:10.628
10 minutes with anyone who's used it?

27
00:01:10.908 --> 00:01:12.871
5-minute technical deep-dive:

28
00:01:13.151 --> 00:01:14.921
Found an interesting caching issue.

29
00:01:15.201 --> 00:01:16.460
I'll share in backend.

30
00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:18.685
Part 2.

31
00:01:18.965 --> 00:01:20.607
Slack or Teams messages.

32
00:01:21.857 --> 00:01:22.924
Golden rules.

33
00:01:23.204 --> 00:01:24.441
Don't just say Hi.

34
00:01:24.721 --> 00:01:26.791
Write the whole question in one message.

35
00:01:27.071 --> 00:01:28.884
Point first, details after.

36
00:01:29.164 --> 00:01:30.145
Use threads.

37
00:01:30.425 --> 00:01:31.663
Don't flood the channel.

38
00:01:31.943 --> 00:01:33.415
Say how urgent it is:

39
00:01:33.695 --> 00:01:37.364
FYI, When you get a chance, or Urgent: blocking the release.

40
00:01:37.644 --> 00:01:38.604
Close the loop:

41
00:01:38.884 --> 00:01:41.828
Resolved, thanks! so nobody else spends time on it.

42
00:01:43.178 --> 00:01:44.522
Here is a quick table:

43
00:01:44.802 --> 00:01:46.061
Instead of, and Write.

44
00:01:46.341 --> 00:01:47.087
Hi...

45
00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:49.223
(waits 10 min)... are you there?:

46
00:01:49.503 --> 00:01:55.391
Hi Ravi, quick one: is the orders topic partitioned by customerId or orderId?

47
00:01:55.671 --> 00:01:58.146
Writing a consumer and want to keep ordering.

48
00:01:58.426 --> 00:01:59.685
The build is broken:

49
00:01:59.965 --> 00:02:06.023
Main build failing since 11:20 on InventoryIT, looks like a Testcontainers timeout.

50
00:02:06.303 --> 00:02:08.202
Looking into it; will update here.

51
00:02:08.482 --> 00:02:09.442
Can we talk?:

52
00:02:09.722 --> 00:02:12.367
Can we talk for 10 min today about the sprint scope?

53
00:02:12.647 --> 00:02:14.738
Nothing urgent, just want to align.

54
00:02:16.088 --> 00:02:16.984
Part 3.

55
00:02:17.264 --> 00:02:18.011
Email.

56
00:02:19.261 --> 00:02:21.138
Here is a template you can copy.

57
00:02:21.418 --> 00:02:22.293
Subject:

58
00:02:22.573 --> 00:02:26.178
Decision needed by Fri Choose payment provider for Q1.

59
00:02:26.458 --> 00:02:27.375
Hi Priya.

60
00:02:27.655 --> 00:02:29.853
Recommendation: go with Razorpay.

61
00:02:30.133 --> 00:02:35.530
Cheaper fees (1.8% versus 2.2%) and the SDK we need.

62
00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:36.983
Options compared:

63
00:02:37.263 --> 00:02:38.415
(table or link).

64
00:02:38.695 --> 00:02:42.855
Risk: migration takes ~2 weeks; I've planned it for early Dec.

65
00:02:43.135 --> 00:02:46.335
Could you confirm by Friday so we can start the integration?

66
00:02:46.615 --> 00:02:47.362
Thanks.

67
00:02:47.642 --> 00:02:48.474
Ashish.

68
00:02:51.324 --> 00:02:54.503
For more templates and tone guidance, see Email Writing.

69
00:02:54.783 --> 00:03:02.889
Tips: the subject line says what you need, the first line gives the answer, under 150 words, one ask, a clear deadline.

70
00:03:04.239 --> 00:03:05.157
Part 4.

71
00:03:05.437 --> 00:03:06.973
Pull request descriptions.

72
00:03:08.223 --> 00:03:09.801
Here is the MARKDOWN code.

73
00:03:10.081 --> 00:03:13.580
It runs to 16 lines; the full listing is in the chapter.

74
00:03:16.430 --> 00:03:17.390
Part 5.

75
00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:18.566
Estimates.

76
00:03:19.816 --> 00:03:21.821
Give ranges, not single numbers:

77
00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:23.360
3 to 5 days.

78
00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:28.120
Say what the estimate assumes:...assuming the API contract doesn't change.

79
00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.619
Re-estimate out loud when things change:

80
00:03:30.899 --> 00:03:31.795
New info.

81
00:03:32.075 --> 00:03:33.995
It's now 7 days, here's why.

82
00:03:34.275 --> 00:03:35.384
I don't know yet.

83
00:03:35.664 --> 00:03:39.803
I'll spike for half a day and give you an estimate tomorrow is a good answer.

84
00:03:41.153 --> 00:03:42.091
Part 6.

85
00:03:42.371 --> 00:03:43.971
Useful everyday phrases.

86
00:03:45.221 --> 00:03:46.565
Here is a quick table:

87
00:03:46.845 --> 00:03:48.232
Situation, and Say.

88
00:03:48.512 --> 00:03:49.792
You didn't understand:

89
00:03:50.072 --> 00:03:51.715
Sorry, could you say that again?

90
00:03:51.995 --> 00:03:53.701
I want to make sure I get it right.

91
00:03:53.981 --> 00:03:54.963
Buying time:

92
00:03:55.243 --> 00:03:56.245
Good question.

93
00:03:56.525 --> 00:03:58.723
Let me check and get back to you by 3.

94
00:03:59.003 --> 00:04:00.176
Polite reminder:

95
00:04:00.456 --> 00:04:01.779
Gentle nudge on this.

96
00:04:02.059 --> 00:04:03.061
Any update?

97
00:04:03.341 --> 00:04:04.429
Saying you're busy:

98
00:04:04.709 --> 00:04:06.715
I'm heads-down on the release till 4.

99
00:04:06.995 --> 00:04:08.296
Can I look after that?

100
00:04:08.576 --> 00:04:09.472
Agreeing:

101
00:04:09.752 --> 00:04:11.480
Makes sense, let's go with that.

102
00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:12.933
Partially agreeing:

103
00:04:13.213 --> 00:04:14.664
I agree with the approach.

104
00:04:14.944 --> 00:04:16.693
One concern about the timeline...

105
00:04:16.973 --> 00:04:18.189
Ending a long call:

106
00:04:18.469 --> 00:04:19.792
I think we've covered it.

107
00:04:20.072 --> 00:04:22.035
I'll send a summary in 10 minutes.

108
00:04:22.315 --> 00:04:23.509
Taking ownership:

109
00:04:23.789 --> 00:04:24.813
I'll own this.

110
00:04:25.093 --> 00:04:27.013
Expect an update by end of day.

111
00:04:28.363 --> 00:04:29.302
Part 7.

112
00:04:29.582 --> 00:04:32.185
End-of-day or weekly update (to manager).

113
00:04:33.435 --> 00:04:35.312
Here is a template you can copy.

114
00:04:35.592 --> 00:04:36.808
Week of 3 Nov.

115
00:04:37.088 --> 00:04:40.501
Done: coupon validation (shipped), fixed 3 cart bugs.

116
00:04:40.781 --> 00:04:45.389
In progress: delivery-slot API (60%), on track for Weds.

117
00:04:45.669 --> 00:04:48.379
Risk: map vendor API key still pending.

118
00:04:48.659 --> 00:04:52.840
Need: decision on slot-caching TTL (5 versus 15 min).

119
00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:56.565
Part 8.

120
00:04:56.845 --> 00:04:58.231
Practice conversation:

121
00:04:58.511 --> 00:04:59.727
Stand-up update.

122
00:05:00.977 --> 00:05:03.004
Here is how the conversation goes.

123
00:05:03.284 --> 00:05:04.713
Ashish, your update?

124
00:05:04.993 --> 00:05:10.412
Yesterday I finished the coupon validation API, and the PR is in review.

125
00:05:10.692 --> 00:05:12.719
Today I'll connect it to the cart.

126
00:05:12.999 --> 00:05:14.193
Any blockers?

127
00:05:14.473 --> 00:05:15.177
One.

128
00:05:15.457 --> 00:05:18.167
I need access to the staging database.

129
00:05:18.447 --> 00:05:20.836
Ravi, could you help after the stand-up?

130
00:05:22.186 --> 00:05:23.786
The conversation continues.

131
00:05:24.066 --> 00:05:25.837
Sure, I'll add you in ten minutes.

132
00:05:26.117 --> 00:05:26.927
Thanks.

133
00:05:27.207 --> 00:05:28.551
That's all from me.

134
00:05:29.901 --> 00:05:31.437
That's the end of this lesson.

135
00:05:31.717 --> 00:05:36.368
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

136
00:05:36.648 --> 00:05:42.771
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

